    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **68 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `ownerSegment` derived field for owners. The change spans three files, following the existing conventions in the codebase:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added the `ownerSegment` read-only property to the `OwnerDto` schema as an enum (`PREMIUM_METRO`, `PREMIUM_REGIONAL`, `STANDARD_METRO`, `STANDARD_REGIONAL`), which drives the build-time generated DTO.\n\n2. **`LocalityLookup.java`** \u2014 Added a `segmentFor(membershipLevel, postcode, city)` helper. It computes:\n   - **TIER**: `PREMIUM` when `membershipLevel >= 3`, else `STANDARD`.\n   - **AREA**: `METRO` when the derived region is a known region (NSW/VIC/QLD), else `REGIONAL`.\n   \n   This keeps the locality logic co-located with the existing `locality`/`timezone` derivations rather than in the `Owner` entity.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Mapping` expression that calls `segmentFor(...)` (using the owner's derived `membershipLevel`) and converts the result via `OwnerDto.OwnerSegmentEnum.fromValue(...)`, mirroring the existing `ageBand` enum mapping.\n\nThe two new `Cp55Tests` pass, and no existing tests regressed.",
